  ('a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000007502', $m$codigo$m$, $m$SP1-928$m$, NULL, $m$Heater OFF During Feeding Heater OFF Time$m$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $m$[5 to 60/60/1]$m$, $m$[5 to 60/60/1]$m$),
  ('a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000007502', $m$codigo$m$, $m$SP1-929-001$m$, NULL, $m$Dev. Bias (Image) Adjusts the development bias for copying when process control is off Adjust as a temporary measure to compensate for an aging drum until the old drum can be replaced.$m$, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $m$[100 to 800/550/10 V]$m$),
  ('a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000007502', $m$codigo$m$, $m$SP1-929-002$m$, NULL, $m$ID Sensor Pattern Adjusts the development bias used to create the ID sensor pattern. DFU This SP and SP2201-004 must be changed together by the same amount.$m$, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $m$[100 to 800/360/10 V]$m$),
  ('a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000007502', $m$codigo$m$, $m$SP1-929-003$m$, NULL, $m$OHP Adjusts the development bias for copying with OHP sheets.$m$, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $m$[100 to 800/300/10 V]$m$),
  ('a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000007502', $m$codigo$m$, $m$SP1-929-004$m$, NULL, $m$ID Sensor Pattern (Dev. Potential) Adjusts the development potential to create the ID sensor pattern. DFU This SP and SP2201-002 must be changed together by the same amount.$m$, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $m$[140 to 380/240/10 V]$m$),
  ('a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000007502', $m$codigo$m$, $m$SP1-929-005$m$, NULL, $m$Vb Target Voltage Sets the Vb target development bias voltage (Vb). DFU$m$, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $m$[100 to 800/550/1 V]$m$),
  ('a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000007502', $m$codigo$m$, $m$SP1-929-006$m$, NULL, $m$Trailing Edge Pixel (Level - 600 dpi)$m$, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000007502', $m$codigo$m$, $m$SP1-929-007$m$, NULL, $m$Continuous Pixel (Level - 600 dpi)$m$, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $m$[2 to 15/15/1]$m$),
  ('a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000007502', $m$codigo$m$, $m$SP1-929-008$m$, NULL, $m$Independent Dot Pixel (Level - 600 dpi) 2115 Main Scan Beam Pitch Adjustment A label attached to the LD unit service part lists the correct settings. Refer to these settings when adjusting the beam pitch for LD0 to LD3.$m$, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000007502', $m$codigo$m$, $m$SP2-207$m$, NULL, $m$Forced Toner Supply$m$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $m$Rotates the toner bottle to supply toner to the toner supply unit. Press Execute to force toner supply. Use to determine if toner supply is operating correctly. If forcing toner supply with this SP does not darken the image, then toner supply is not operating correctly.$m$, NULL),
  ('a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000007502', $m$codigo$m$, $m$SP2-208$m$, NULL, $m$Toner Supply Mode$m$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $m$Selects the toner supply mode: Sensor Control or Image Pixel Count. [0 to 1/0/1] 0: Sensor Control 1: Pixel Count Select Image Pixel Count only if the TD sensor has failed and cannot be replaced immediately, so that the customer can use the machine. Return the setting to Sensor Control after replacing the sensor.$m$, $m$[0 to 1/0/1]$m$),
  ('a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000007502', $m$codigo$m$, $m$SP2-209$m$, NULL, $m$Toner Supply Rate$m$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $m$Adjusts the toner supply rate. Program [50 to 2000/850/5 mg per sec] Increasing this value reduces the time the toner supply clutch remains on. Use Mode Tables a lower value if the user tends to make many copies that have large areas of black.$m$, $m$[50 to 2000/850/5 mg per sec]$m$),
  ('a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000007502', $m$codigo$m$, $m$SP2-210$m$, NULL, $m$ID Sensor Pattern Interval$m$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $m$Adjusts the time interval between making ID sensor patterns onto the drum for Vsp/Vsg detection. [0 to 200/10/1] Reduce the interval for copies that contain a high proportion of black.$m$, $m$[0 to 200/10/1]$m$),
  ('a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000007502', $m$codigo$m$, $m$SP2-220$m$, NULL, $m$Vref Manual Setting$m$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $m$Adjusts the TD sensor reference voltage (Vref) manually. [1 to 4/2.5/0.01 V] Change this value after replacing the development unit with another one that already contains toner. For example, when using a development unit from another machine for test purposes, do the following: Check the value of SP2220 in both the machine containing the test unit and the machine that you are going to move it to. Install the test development unit, then input the VREF for this unit into SP2220. After the test, put back the old development unit, and change SP2220 back to the original value.$m$, $m$[1 to 4/2.5/0.01 V]$m$),
  ('a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000007502', $m$codigo$m$, $m$SP2-223-001$m$, NULL, $m$Operation Mode Program Determines whether the charge corona wire is cleaned at regular intervals. Mode Tables 0: No 1: Yes The time interval between cleaning is set with SP2804-002.$m$, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $m$[0 to 1/1]$m$),
  ('a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000007502', $m$codigo$m$, $m$SP2-223-002$m$, NULL, $m$Number of Sheets Sets the interval (number of sheets printed) between charge corona wire cleanings. 2901 Humidity Control 0: OFF 1:ON Humidity Thresh: Trans. Bias$m$, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $m$[100 to 10,000/5000/100] [0 or 1/ 0 / -] [0 to 100 / 70 / 1%]$m$),
